<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Filing Your Tax Return</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">You may file your tax return any time before the extension expires. But, remember, Form 4868 does not extend the time to pay your tax. If you do not pay your tax by the regular due date, you will owe interest. You may also be charged penalties.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Do not attach a copy of Form 4868 to your return.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">If you have already paid your tax, we have included an extra copy of Form 4868. However, only file one.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">How To Claim Credit for Payment Made With This Form</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">When you file your return, include the amount of any payment you sent with Form 4868 on line 10 of your tax return. If you file Form 1040EZ, the instructions for line 10 tell you how to report the payment. If you file Form 1040, enter the payment on line 61. If you file Form 1040NR-EZ, see the instructions for line 22. If you file Form 1040NR, see the instructions for line 22.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">If you and your spouse each filed a separate Form 4868 but file a joint return for 1998, enter the total paid with both Forms 4868 on the appropriate line of your joint return. You and your spouse may divide the payment in any agreed amounts. Be sure each separate return has the social security numbers of both spouses.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="divider"></div>

    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Specific Instructions</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Part I Identification</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Enter your name(s) and address. If you plan to file a joint return, include both spouses' names in the order in which they appear on your joint return.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">If you want correspondence regarding this extension to be sent to an address other than your own or to another person, you must provide the agent's name, if any, and enter that address.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Part II Individual Income Tax</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">If you changed your name after you filed your last return, you must use your new name on this form. If you are filing a joint return, you must use the name that appears on your joint return.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">If you are filing a joint return, you must use the name that appears on your joint return. If you are filing a joint return, you must use the name that appears on your joint return.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Part III Gift/GST Tax</p>
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">If you are filing a gift or GST tax return, you must use the name that appears on that return.</p>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start;">
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Part IV Total</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">Enter the total of line 6 and 7, if applicable on line 9. If you are filing your entire estimate of tax liability, lines 9 and 10 should both be the same.</p>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <h3 style="margin-top: 0;">Privacy Act and Paperwork Reduction Act Notice</h3>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">We use this information to carry out our internal revenue tax return within months after the regular due date. If you are filing a joint return, we will use the names of both spouses. We use this information to carry out our internal revenue tax return within months after the regular due date. If you are filing a joint return, we will use the names of both spouses.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">The information requested on this form is used for tax administration purposes only. It will not be shared with any other agency or entity.</p>
            <p style="font-size: 10pt;">If you have comments concerning the accuracy of these time extensions, please write them on the bottom of this form and mail it to the IRS address listed in the instructions.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 30px;">
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">For more information, please see the instructions for Form 4868. You can also download forms from the IRS Internet web site at www.irs.gov.</p>
    </div>

    <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
        <p style="font-size: 10pt;">[ ] This is an extra copy. File only one Form 4868.</p>
